BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mary Oliver: Saved by the Beauty of the World
DTSTART:20260727T224500Z
DTEND:20260728T003500Z
DTSTAMP:20260727T224500Z
UID:q38kOiXrIJ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 91 mins (1h31m)\n\nMary Oliver – best-selling poet
  and Pulitzer Prize-winner\; lover of dogs and long walks in the woods\; q
 ueer and out\, but intensely private. Her poems inspire liberals and conse
 rvatives\, atheists and believers\, naturalists and urbanites. If poetry h
 ad a pop icon\, Mary Oliver would be it. Featuring poems read by Helena Bo
 nham Carter\, Steve Buscemi\, Stephen Colbert\, Lucy Dacus\, Jesse Welles\
 , and Oprah Winfrey.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/mary-olive
 r-saved-by-the-beauty-of-the-world\n\nEstimated start: 16:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Piano (1993)
DTSTART:20260727T230000Z
DTEND:20260728T011500Z
DTSTAMP:20260727T230000Z
UID:cGCtW1QhZq
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 117 mins (1h57m)\n\n1851. Ada has never spoken a wor
 d since the age of six and only communicates through music and her daughte
 r\, Flora. An arranged marriage forces her to leave her native Scotland wi
 th her daughter and her piano. Her destination is New Zealand\, where she 
 is awaited by Stewart\, a farmer with whom she has nothing in common. Her 
 suffering only gets worse when her husband sells the piano to his neighbou
 r George. But Ada will find a way to continue playing in exchange for givi
 ng George lessons. New 4K Restoration.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-t
 heaters/the-piano\n\nEstimated start: 16:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
