SUMMARY:Maddie's Secret
DTSTART:20260730T233000Z
DTEND:20260731T013500Z
DTSTAMP:20260730T233000Z
UID:hligwYA7XQ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 108 mins (1h48m)\n\nUnmissable directorial debut sat
 irizing and skewering content culture from iconic alt-comedian John Early\
 , who plays the titular role\, alongside a troupe of comedians including K
 ate Berlant\, Vanessa Bayer\, and Conner O’Malley.  From July 17 to 19\,
  all 7:00pm screenings will include a pre-recorded Q&A with John Early and
  one of these special guests:July 17 - Amy SedarisJuly 18 - Hannah Einbind
 erJuly 19 - Sarah Sherman\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/maddi
 es-secret-yr\n\nEstimated start: 16:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Honeyjoon
DTSTART:20260731T013000Z
DTEND:20260731T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20260731T013000Z
UID:9BRZCv3XAx
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 75 mins (1h15m)\n\nIn this light-and-dark comedy\, J
 une and her Persian mom Lela travel to the Azores islands for a grief anni
 versary\, with contrasting ways of coping. A charming surfer brings balanc
 e as they (and we) surf the waves of life\, loss\, flirting… an unforget
 table ride. Director Lilian T. Mehrel scheduled to attend for a post-film
  Q&A on July 17\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/honeyjoon\n\nEs
 timated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sorry to Bother You (2018)
DTSTART:20260731T020000Z
DTEND:20260731T041000Z
DTSTAMP:20260731T020000Z
UID:Q331Q5w5Kq
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nLakeith Stanfield\, Tessa Thomps
 on\, and Steven Yeun star in the exhilarating directorial debut of musicia
 n Boots Riley\, a biting and bonkers satire that follows a black telemarke
 ter who discovers an unknown skill which gives him magical selling powers 
 that shoot him up the corporate ladder. Includes a pre-recorded introducti
 on and post-film Q&A with Art House Theater Day Ambassador Boots Riley!\n\
 nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/art-house-theater-day-2026/sorry
 -to-bother-you\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Piano (1993)
DTSTART:20260731T021500Z
DTEND:20260731T043000Z
DTSTAMP:20260731T021500Z
UID:CsseewtiSf
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 117 mins (1h57m)\n\n1851. Ada has never spoken a wor
 d since the age of six and only communicates through music and her daughte
 r\, Flora. An arranged marriage forces her to leave her native Scotland wi
 th her daughter and her piano. Her destination is New Zealand\, where she 
 is awaited by Stewart\, a farmer with whom she has nothing in common. Her 
 suffering only gets worse when her husband sells the piano to his neighbou
 r George. But Ada will find a way to continue playing in exchange for givi
 ng George lessons. New 4K Restoration.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-t
 heaters/the-piano\n\nEstimated start: 19:30
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
