SUMMARY:North by Northwest (1959)
DTSTART:20260920T180000Z
DTEND:20260920T203500Z
DTSTAMP:20260920T180000Z
UID:54IHle64VE
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 136 mins (2h16m)\n\nCommunity ScreeningsCary Grant s
 tars as an innocent man mistaken for a spy in one of Alfred Hitchcock's gr
 eatest thrillers. While leaving New York's Plaza Hotel\, advertising execu
 tive Roger Thornhill (Grant) has the misfortune of standing just as the na
 me "George Kaplan" is paged--starting a lethal case of mistaken identity a
 nd a nonstop game of cat and mouse as he is pursued across North America b
 y espionage agents trying to kill him--and by police who suspect him of mu
 rder.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/community-screenings/nor
 th-by-northwest\n\nEstimated start: 11:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jules and Jim (1961)
DTSTART:20260924T020000Z
DTEND:20260924T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20260924T020000Z
UID:DyvIK0gD7D
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 105 mins (1h45m)\n\nNouvelles FemmesTwo Parisian lit
 erature-loving friends (Oscar Werner\, Henri Serre) are dumbstruck when th
 ey encounter Catherine (Jeanne Moreau)\, a real-life embodiment of passion
 ate\, adventurous living. Respect and affection flow freely between the th
 ree\, and soon a larking-about friendship branches into many configuration
 s of love.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/nouvelles-femmes/ju
 les-and-jim\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cleo From 5 to 7 (1962)
DTSTART:20261001T020000Z
DTEND:20261001T034500Z
DTSTAMP:20261001T020000Z
UID:1wqNomEtwX
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nNouvelles FemmesThis afternoon\, 
 beautiful pop singer Cléo (Corinne Marchand) will find out the results of
  her cancer biopsy\, and this raw fact changes her life. She’s used to e
 veryone looking adoringly at her\, defining her as a princess. Today\, as 
 Varda says\, “She changes to a black dress\, like singer Edith Piaf\, an
 d goes out\; now she looks at the world.”\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/progra
 ms-and-events/nouvelles-femmes/cleo-from-5-to-7\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Contempt (1963)
DTSTART:20261008T020000Z
DTEND:20261008T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20261008T020000Z
UID:R5NOmEaDHN
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nNouvelles FemmesA film producer 
 (Jack Palance) and his director (pantheon director Fritz Lang) are filming
  Homer’s The Odyssey. The screenwriter (Michel Piccoli) and his stunning
  wife (Brigitte Bardot) are on the scene. Godard seeks to “film thought\
 , the beauty of moments\,” and a small emotional miscalculation (or happ
 enstance) sows doubt in a Mediterranean paradise.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/
 programs-and-events/nouvelles-femmes/contempt\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
